{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe rain here has been relentless since Sunday, yet I could not resist the damp. I took a carriage to the Augarten and on to Nussdorf, where the air was thick and heavy. Along the road, I stopped before a large pear tree. Its fruit had already been gathered, yet there, against all reason, it stood in full bloom again.\n\nIt struck me with a strange force: the tree, having given its substance, now returns to its first, most delicate state. It is a kind of life that refuses to be exhausted by its own productivity. I have enclosed two of these blossoms in this letter. They are fragile, but they carry the scent of that impossible recurrence.\n\nThe journey is tiring, but the mind is clear. I think of you and the boys often. When will I be back to sit by our fireside?\n\nYour loving husband,\nG.W.F."}}],"created":1795080433,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":193,"prompt_tokens":938,"total_tokens":1131,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-j44vcPCgdPjOATO0YYWq6wesiTyrnWF7","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":938,"prompt_ms":1059.27,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.1292857142857142,"prompt_per_second":885.5154965211891,"predicted_n":193,"predicted_ms":4603.812,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.9781875,"predicted_per_second":41.70457003891558}}